@page {
    route: "/embedded-languages/",
    draft: Bool.false,
    theme: "rocci",
    meta: {
        title: "Embedded Languages Demo 🚀",
        description: "Demonstrating every region context in Rocdown 🌟",
    },
}

@roc {
Status : [Active(U64), Idle]

items = [
    { id: 1, name: "Item 1 🚀" },
    { id: 2, name: "Item 2 ✨" },
]
status = Active(42)
isLoaded = True
}

@css {
    .docs-banner {
        background: #f0f4f8;
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 8px;
        border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6;
    }

    .code-highlight {
        color: #0066cc;
        font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
    }
}

@component
Card = |{ title, count ?? 0 }|
    <div class="card">
        <h3>{title}</h3>
        <p>Count: {count.to_str()}</p>
    </div>

@fixture{target: Card}
cardSample = {
    title: "Sample Card 🎴",
    count: 42,
}

# Embedded Languages Test Suite 🌐

Welcome to the comprehensive embedded language test suite for Rocdown. This document
exercises every structural, executable, display-only, and metadata region.

Email docs@example.com for questions, or mention @roclang on community channels.

## Section 1: Typography and Formatting {#sec-typography}

Here is standard prose featuring **bold text**, *italic text*, and ~~strikethrough~~.
Inline code looks like `Num.toStr(42)`. You can also visit [External Link](https://example.com).

- Unordered item 🍎
- Unordered item 🍌
  - Nested item 🍒

1. Ordered step 1 🚀
2. Ordered step 2 🌟

- [x] Completed task item 🎉
- [ ] Incomplete task item ⏳

> "Rocci bridges host Markdown documents with type-safe Roc execution." — Rocci Guide

| Feature | Kind | Status | Emoji |
| :--- | :--- | :---: | ---: |
| Roc | Executable | Active | 🚀 |
| CSS | Stylesheet | Active | 🎨 |
| HTML | Structure | Active | 🌐 |

---

## Section 2: Documentation Components {#sec-docs}

@docs note {
    title: "Important Usage Note",
    open: Bool.true

This is the content of the note. It supports *Markdown* and `inline code`.
}

@docs tabs {
    group: "platform",
    kind: "platform"

    @docs tab {
        id: "mac",
        label: "macOS 🍎"

Run on macOS:

```sh
cargo run -- mac
```
    }

    @docs tab {
        id: "linux",
        label: "Linux 🐧"

Run on Linux:

```sh
cargo run -- linux
```
    }
}

@docs include {
    path: "AllSyntax.rocci",
    language: "rocci"
}

@docs example {
    name: "counter-test",
    command: "cargo test",
    language: "roc"

```roc
counter = 42
```
}

@docs link-card {
    page: "/guides/getting-started/",
    title: "Getting Started 🚀",
    description: "Learn how to build applications with Rocci."
}

@docs details {
    summary: "Advanced Details 🔍",
    open: Bool.false

Here is collapsible markdown content that stays hidden until expanded.
}

## Section 3: Display-Only Code Fences {#sec-fences}

The following code blocks are display-only and must never be executed or treated as executable islands:

```roc
# Ordinary display-only Roc fence
main = \{} -> "Hello from display Roc!"
```

```html
<div class="display-container">
    <p>Raw HTML snippet for display only &amp; entities</p>
</div>
```

```css
.display-class {
    color: #10b981;
    font-size: 1rem;
}
```

```sh
rocci build --release
```

```text
Plain inert text block 📝
```

## Section 4: Executable Island and Template Directives {#sec-executable}

@render {
    card({ title: "Rendered Card 🎉", count: 100 })
}

@let activeItems = List.keep_if(items, |item| item.id > 0)

@if isLoaded {
    <p>Data loaded successfully! 🌟</p>
} @else if List.is_empty(activeItems) {
    <p>No active items available.</p>
} @else {
    <p>Loading pending... ⏳</p>
}

@for item in activeItems {
    <li>{item.name}</li>
}

@match status {
    Active(n) => <p>Active count: {n.to_str()}</p>
    Idle => <p>System is currently idle 💤</p>
}

## Section 5: Escaped Syntax and Edge Cases {#sec-escapes}

\@docs note { this is escaped and not a real directive }

\@if this is also escaped

More trailing markdown with non-BMP Gothic character 𐍈 and emojis 🌈✨.
